A||N||2||fastback87||87 GT fastback Auto to Manual Swap???||||5||
Z||000000||fastback87||10-23-2001||05:33 PM||||Does anyone know what it takes to swap an automatic tranny with a Manual on an 87 V6??  I can find all kinds of manuals that are in 2m4's and am not sure if they are the same or which ones are better than others.  I can do the mechanical swap no problem, the problem is when it comes time to install and hook up the new linkage and electrical differences between the auto's and manual's.  can I just swap the wiring harness from another v6 manual into my auto?  I just want to know what kind of chore this is going to be.  Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||88CoupeV6||10-23-2001||05:44 PM||||I think you can use any v6 manual harness. I know I used a 4 speed harness from a 86 V6 with my 5 speed isuzu trans. everything plugged in.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||10-23-2001||07:58 PM||||The tranny that is in the 2M4's are not the same tranny installed in the factory V-6 cars. They can be used and will bolt up, <BR>V-8Archie uses them in V-8 swaps. Rumor has it that they wont take much 'gear slapping' but the hold up well behind the V-8's.<BR>Any manual V-6 harness will work. You will need to obtain a PROM for the setup of your choosing.<P>Happy Fieroing!  LOL||||reg||1
